@startuml sequence-service-token
title Service token: only a platform service gets in (every endpoint except actuator, OpenAPI, Swagger UI)

actor "Client" as Client
participant "individuals-api" as IA
participant "Keycloak" as KC
box "transaction-service" #F5F9FF
    participant "SecurityConfig\n(resource server)" as Sec
    participant "GlobalExceptionHandler" as Err
    participant "Controller -> Service" as App
    database "DB (shard by user_uid)" as DB
end box

Client -> IA: request with the user's Bearer token
IA -> IA: user's token checked, user_uid taken from it\n(as in the endpoint's own sequence)
alt service token cached and valid for more than 10 s
    IA -> IA: take it from the cache
else no token yet or it is about to expire
    IA -> KC: POST /realms/{realm}/protocol/openid-connect/token\ngrant_type=client_credentials, client individuals-api, secret from .env
    alt Keycloak unavailable or 5xx
        KC --> IA: no answer / 5xx
        IA --> Client: 503 DEPENDENCY_UNAVAILABLE
        note right of IA: transaction-service is not called
    else token issued
        KC --> IA: access token: azp individuals-api,\nrealm_access.roles [SERVICE]
        IA -> IA: cache it until 10 s before expiry
    end
end
IA -> Sec: request + Authorization: Bearer <service token> + X-User-Uid
Sec -> KC: GET /realms/{realm}/protocol/openid-connect/certs\n(on the first token, then cached; again for an unknown key id)
alt no Authorization header
    Sec -> Err: AuthenticationException
    Err --> IA: 401 AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED
else signature not by the realm keys, malformed or expired
    Sec -> Err: AuthenticationException
    Err --> IA: 401 AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED
else valid token without the realm role SERVICE (a user's token)
    Sec -> Err: AccessDeniedException
    Err --> IA: 403 ACCESS_DENIED
else valid token with the realm role SERVICE
    Sec -> App: the request
    App -> DB: as in the endpoint's own sequence
    App --> IA: the endpoint's answer
end
note over Sec, DB
  401 / 403: no controller is reached, nothing is read or written, no money moves.
  X-User-Uid is trusted only after this check.
  iss is not compared (jwk-set-uri, not issuer-uri): individuals-api asks keycloak:8080,
  Postman asks localhost:8080, and the signature by the realm keys already proves the issuer.
end note
alt 401 or 403 from transaction-service
    IA --> Client: 500 INTERNAL_ERROR, their body only in the log:\nour configuration is wrong (role or Keycloak address), not the client's request
else the endpoint's answer
    IA --> Client: as in the endpoint's own sequence
end
@enduml
